// [DOOM] Zero-copy guest memory ("as on Switch"): NVN memory pools are guest memory both the CPU and the GPU address. Here a
// pool's pages are replaced, at nvnMemoryPoolInitialize, by AHardwareBuffer (dma-buf) pages mapped at the very same guest
// addresses, and a VkBuffer is bound over each 64 MB chunk. Buffer reads (vertex, index, uniform, read-only storage, indirect)
// then bind the guest memory itself instead of a per-draw snapshot copy (no copy, hash, page protection or write tracking).
// GPU writes still land through the pending-writeback path. Pages the replay writes on the CPU while earlier recorded draws may
// still read them (UpdateUniformBuffer, CPU buffer copies and clears) become "sticky" and keep the snapshot path.
