// [DOOM] Position invariance between the depth pre-pass and the shading passes. The main pass tests depth for equality with
// the pre-pass result, so both vertex shaders must compute bit-identical positions; NVN's compiler gave that, the Adreno
// compiler may fuse multiply-adds differently in two programs (holes and missing triangles where the test fails). Vertex
// (and tessellation / geometry) shaders get NoContraction on every float arithmetic result and Invariant on Position. The
// translated shaders compute positions with GLSL.std.450 Fma (from Maxwell FFMA); an Fma without NoContraction may also be split
// into a multiply and an add, so it gets the decoration too.
