// [DOOM] DOOM's triangle-culling geometry shaders (703f1fcc3cda7204 + 5 siblings; xbg_spirv_lone.cpp has the test layout).
// They compact visible triangles per Maxwell warp: lane 0 reserves popcount(ballot.x)*3 index slots with one atomic add and
// a 5-step SHFL.UP prefix sum (deltas 1..16) gives every lane its offset. Both assume a warp of exactly 32 lanes, one
// primitive per lane. Where the device runs subgroup operations in geometry shaders (Turnip: stages 0x3f, subgroups of 64 /
