// 与 Metal 侧（nvn_mtl.m 的 first_draw_covers）同一套条件与同一个纯函数 nvn_cover.h（单测 t_cover.c），位置从这次绘制
// 实际交给 GPU 的顶点 / 索引快照里读。不成立就照旧 LOAD。
// Vertex count and full viewport/scissor do not prove full pixel coverage: a partial triangle qualifies. So the old contents
// are skipped only when the geometry proves it: the conditions of the Metal side (nvn_mtl.m's first_draw_covers) and the same
// pure function nvn_cover.h (unit test t_cover.c), with the positions read from the vertex and index snapshots this draw
// hands to the GPU. Otherwise LOAD as before. Explicit clears keep their separate clear semantics.
// The first draw of a pass covers every pixel of each color attachment, writing it without blending: the vertex position
// is one input as it is (XbgRasterFacts), the fragment shader declares every attachment's output, never discards and does
// not write SampleMask, no depth (except ALWAYS), stencil or depth-bounds test, fill mode, single sample, 2D targets, and
// nvn_cover holds for the viewport, scissor, culling (the NVN cull and front face, as the Metal side passes them) and
// vertices. Should its winding reading ever differ from the GPU's, the visible triangle reads as culled and the pass simply
// loads. noload_why counts the first failing check:
// 0 shaders, 1 attachment state, 2 depth/stencil, 3 raster state (also: covered but culled), 4 primitive/count,
// 5 position format/stream, 6 vertex/index read, 7 geometry.
// [DOOM] DM_GFX_TAA_FIX (bit mask, default 2 since the owner's play test of 28.10: no indoor fog haze, decals no longer
// flicker with the view, no dropped triangles, better reflections; read once, fixed for the run; work/research/taa_fix.md):
//  1 = TAA probe. At the fragment TAA resolve (taa_vsps, ps 615e5352a9db7427, once a frame) log its five inputs (slot 0
//      depth, 1 object velocity, 2 current colour, 3 pre-transparency colour for transparency_k, 4 history), their images
//      and samplers, the targets, and the uniforms that define the reprojection; count frames whose history input is not
//      the previous frame's TAA output (a broken history chain never converges).
//  2 = NVN lower-left window origin. DOOM sets the depth mode but never calls nvnDeviceSetWindowOriginMode, so it runs
//      with NVN's default LOWER_LEFT (GL) origin: texel row 0 holds NDC y = -1, and its Switch-only shaders depend on that
//      (GS occlusion culling: Hi-Z texel = (ndc * 0.5 + 0.5) * 720; motion vectors and TAA reprojection:
//      tc = ndc * 0.5 + 0.5 against texel rows; the cluster grid and shadow atlas the CPU fills in GL terms). The viewport
//      xbg_nvn_viewport builds is D2R's UPPER_LEFT mapping (NDC +1 -> row 0), so all of those read vertically mirrored
//      texels. Mode 2 uses a positive-height viewport (NDC -1 -> row y, rows then match the Switch's), swaps the front face
//      (Vulkan's polygon area has the opposite sign of GL's for the same window coordinates; the mirrored viewport
//      cancelled that) and presents the window texture blitted upside down, as the Switch displays a lower-left window.
//      Off while the HarmonyOS UI shift is registered (its scissor / viewport offsets assume the mirrored rows).
