// pass-through (Shader::gs_gate_slot) and whose switch word is off at replay time runs without the geometry stage. In the open
// Mars scenes that is ~400 depth pre-pass draws a frame (r_geometryCulling 0): no GS pass on the GPU, and without the GS's two
// written storage buffers the draw's descriptor set is memoized (setcache why=dm ~410/frame -> 0; ~18 us CPU each). The word
// is read from guest memory as uniform_snapshot would (UpdateUniformBuffer already applied in replay order); a pending GPU
// result over it keeps the GS. With culling on (word == 1) nothing changes. Counters: NVN PERF gs_passthru.
